-## Scene 4 — Define the boundary
-<!-- claim_id: 01-c4 -->
+### Scene 4 — Clear boundaries, limited comparisons
+<!-- 01-c3 -->
+<!-- 01-c4 -->
 
 **Narration**
 
-The solar-segmentation protocol makes the boundaries concrete. The agent may edit only the training program. It cannot edit the evaluator and never trains on validation or test images. Each campaign is capped at 24 logged experiments, including the baseline. The one-hour allowance applies to an individual training trial, not the entire campaign. For a student planning a small experiment, this is a useful example of specifying the permitted changes, evaluation boundary, and trial budget before starting.
+The solar-panel segmentation study makes the boundaries explicit. Agents may edit the training program, but cannot edit the evaluator or train on validation or test images. Each campaign allows twenty-four logged experiments, including the baseline.
+
+The limitations matter just as much. Every proposed change uses one random seed. Loops A and C have no test evaluation. Coding model and GPU class vary together. Our inference is that these results cannot identify a generally superior coding model or training recipe.
 
 **Visual**
 
-Editable box: **Training program**. Locked boxes: **Evaluator**, **Validation/test images excluded from training**. Budget cards: **24 experiments per campaign, baseline included**; **3,600 seconds per training trial**. Label the final recommendation **Interpretation**.
+Show an editable “Training program” box beside a locked “Evaluator” box, with a counter capped at “24, including baseline.” Then show three limitation cards. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10491), §2 “Method”: “The agent may edit only the training program”; §3, limitation paragraph before §4: “The coding model is confounded with GPU class”. Label the comparative conclusion **Inference**.
 
-[Source: Solar segmentation](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10491), §2 **Method**. Exact excerpt locators: “The agent may edit only the training program”; “the validation IoU after 3600 s.”; “Each campaign is capped at 24 logged experiments, including the baseline.”
